## Live image with a lean Hyprland (Wayland) desktop + Shinobi OS agent tooling
##
## Built via: distro/build.sh --variant shinobi
##
## The pre-Quickshell desktop baseline built successfully on 2026-09-14. A
## fresh full-image build is required before releasing this revised package
## set. One real bug found and fixed by that build: lxqt-policykit has a hard
## `Depends: lxqt-session`, not just a
## recommendation, which registered a second, competing session with SDDM
## and made it possible to end up in an LXQt session instead of Hyprland.
## Replaced with hyprpolkitagent — a Hyprland-native polkit agent with no
## session dependency at all (just Qt6/QML libs).

## Live images always want these
kali-linux-core

## Graphical desktop — Hyprland (Wayland compositor). No kali-desktop-hyprland
## metapackage exists upstream (unlike xfce/gnome/kde/i3/...), so the stack
## is listed explicitly instead of pulling in Kali's desktop metapackage.
hyprland
xdg-desktop-portal
xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland
xdg-desktop-portal-gtk
quickshell
wofi
hypridle
hyprlock
hyprpolkitagent
swaybg
grim
slurp
wl-clipboard
cliphist
mako-notifier
libnotify-bin
kitty
sddm
plymouth
pipewire
wireplumber
pipewire-pulse
bluez
network-manager

## The Shinobi Installation Wizard, launched from the boot menu's "Install
## Shinobi OS" entry. On the live image only: it is shinobi-installer's Depends
## rather than shinobi-desktop's, because an installed system has no use for
## Qt6 and the KPM partition libraries, and a CLI or headless install should not
## carry a graphical installer it will never run.
calamares

## What an unpackfs install needs that the live session does not. The installed system
## is a byte copy of this image's squashfs, so the bootloader's modules and the
## filesystem tools have to be in the image. (The ISO's own boot loaders are installed
## by live-build after the squashfs is made and are not in it, and Kali's ISO uses the
## Debian installer, so nothing here ever needed these.) Found by running the wizard:
## `grub-install` failed with "/usr/lib/grub/i386-pc/modinfo.sh doesn't exist".
##
## grub-pc-bin and grub-efi-amd64-bin, not grub-pc / grub-efi-amd64: the metapackages
## Conflict with each other and own /etc/default/grub through their postinst scripts,
## and Calamares runs grub-install itself. The cost is that GRUB's boot code is not
## refreshed by upgrades; the installed system keeps the core image it was installed
## with.
grub-pc-bin
grub-efi-amd64-bin
## FAT32 for the EFI System Partition: the wizard formats a new one with mkfs.fat.
dosfstools
## The wizard's "install alongside" flow can only shrink an NTFS partition with these.
ntfs-3g
## grub-install registers the boot entry itself in current GRUB, but efibootmgr is what
## Calamares' bootloader module and Debian's installer both expect to be there.
efibootmgr

## Fonts — a Nerd Font is fetched directly from upstream by
## hooks/live/0030-fonts.chroot (see that file for why); these are just its
## build-time dependencies.
curl
unzip
fontconfig

## shinobi-hypr-toggle (gaps/opacity toggles) parses `hyprctl -j` output.
jq
btop

## Shinobi OS runtime deps — the shinobi CLI itself is installed by
## variant-shinobi/hooks/live/0020-shinobi-tooling.chroot, not apt.
python3-venv
python3-pip
rsync
dbus-user-session


## Extra Kali packages/tools/applications
##   For the complete list see: https://www.kali.org/tools/
##                              https://pkg.kali.org/
#<package>
